<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip Julius, Duke of Pomerania-Wolgast</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1584">1584</a>–<a href="/years/1625">1625</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip Julius (1584–1625) was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a> from 1592, at first under the guardianship of his uncle. He travelled widely in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> as a young man and later quarrelled with his estates and with the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a>. When he died childless in 1625, Pomerania-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolgast">Wolgast</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-xiv">Bogislaw XIV</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a>, who reunited the duchy.</p></div>
